The main purpose of this position is to assist with the development of policies related to the resolution of financial institutions and to assist with the development of resolution plans.
Detailed Description
The successful candidate will be responsible for the following key performance areas:
Conduct research and draft policies related to the resolution functions of the South African Reserve Bank (SARB).
Draft plans and assess the operational preparedness of the financial institutions in resolution.
Analyse data submitted by financial institutions for the purpose of developing resolution plans and conducting resolvability assessments, and present findings to the Senior Resolution Planning Specialist.
Identify information gaps and develop proposals to address them.
Ascertain and interpret industry-wide issues associated with the coordination and management of a failing financial institution, as well as the risks posed by such a failure.
Participate in engagements with financial institutions and industry stakeholders on issues related to resolution.
Identify and highlight impediments to orderly resolutions, and facilitate internal and/or external meetings to review these and develop recommendations for the SARB Executive.
Stay abreast of international best practices and sector developments, analyse the implications of these changes for the work of the Resolution Planning Division, and make proposals on how these developments might be applied to improve current practices.
Prepare presentations to various SARB and industry forums on matters related to resolution.
Execute the day-to-day activities of the division.
Job Requirements
To be considered for this position, candidates must be in possession of:
a minimum of an Honours degree in Economics or an equivalent qualification; and
a minimum of five years’ job-related experience with a background in economics and/or accounting.
Additional requirements include:
a good understanding of investment analysis, valuations and liquidity management;
in-depth knowledge of regulatory frameworks and international standards;
an understanding of, and experience in, crisis management;
proven experience in risk reporting and/or intelligence gathering in the supervision of banks;
an understanding of financial market infrastructures (FMIs);
knowledge of, or experience in, managing distressed assets;
experience in mergers and acquisitions;
proven facilitation and presentation skills;
strong interpersonal skills;
strong communication skills (verbal and written); and
proficiency in the use of Microsoft (MS) Office products such as MS Word, Excel and PowerPoint.
go to method of application »

The main purpose of this position is to provide specialised technical expertise and recommendations on Microsoft 365 products and services, and to provide third-level support for Microsoft Exchange Online while ensuring its optimum availability and performance as well as troubleshooting problem areas in a timely and accurate manner.
Detailed Description
The successful candidate will be responsible for the following key performance areas:
Design, configure, test and deploy Microsoft 365 and Microsoft Exchange Online products and services.
Provide maintenance and third-level support services on all Microsoft 365 products and services to ensure continued availability and performance of the technologies.
Troubleshoot and perform root-cause analysis related to Microsoft 365 products and services.
Manage the technology life-cycle on all Microsoft 365 and Microsoft Exchange Online products and services.
Implement and maintain the governance and security model for the platform as developed by the Cyber and Information Security Unit at the South African Reserve Bank (SARB).
Proactively monitor and report on Microsoft 365 products and services for their availability and reliability.
Provide periodic reports on the health, usage, performance and life-cycle status of the platform.
Develop , maintain and document technical standards, procedures, user guides, standard operating procedures, instructional documents etc. relating to the Microsoft 365 and Microsoft Exchange Online products and services according to best practice to ensure continuity.
Collaborate and engage with internal and external stakeholders to ensure the functionality of the deployed technologies.
Remediate any security vulnerabilities identified on the platform.
Stay abreast of new developments in Microsoft technologies.
Job Requirements
To be considered for this position, candidates must be in possession of:
the minimum of a Bachelor’s degree (NQF 7) in Information Technology (IT) or an equivalent qualification;
a Microsoft 365 Certificate in Exchange Online Support Engineer Speciality; and
the minimum of 5–7 years of experience in an IT support environment and in managing and administering a Microsoft Exchange Online environment.
Additional requirements include:
industry, organisational and business awareness;
continued learning and/or professional development;
effective communication ;
conceptual thinking;
building and managing relationships;
flexibility;
a drive for results;
experience working in a team-oriented, collaborative environment;
the ability to prioritise and execute tasks in a high-pressure environment;
judgement and decision-making skills;
analysis and problem-solving skills;
resilience;
a service and stakeholder focus; and
the ability to function independently (being a self-starter).

About the job:
The CSIR has a vacancy for a Senior Researcher in the Energy Centre within the Smart Places cluster. The incumbent will be responsible for supporting energy economic modelling research area within the CSIR Energy Centre. This research area will gather, create and provide objective information and analysis on energy economics. This will include developing economic models for different energy sources and systems. The incumbent also support the translation of CSIR energy-related research into direct and tangible recommendations for South African industries on how they should position themselves in the energy value chain, and for South African policymakers on how to support South African energy industries and plan and execute a just energy transition.
Key responsibilities:
Responsible for financial and economic modelling for the energy sector (Techno-economics development);
Conduct quantitative and qualitative research techniques in the energy sector;
Assist in forming the research agenda/plan for the Just Energy Transition (JET) in the Energy Centre;
Provide thought-leadership on possible strategy interventions for growing the South African energy industry, specifically in the renewable energy domain;
Advise both internal and external (public and private) industries on the best positioning in the energy value chain localisation;
Participate in development of the CSIR “Optimal Local Content” programme to continuously determine optimal local content levels for different energy technologies;
Compile technical reports for clients in the energy sector;
Establish and maintain relationships/partnership with other leaders locally and globally;
Assist in collecting data for purposes of economic modelling;
Developing economic models to determine job creation, economic growth and supporting benefits of low-carbon energy technologies;
Prepare and deliver presentations to communicate results of studies;
Source and manage contract research and development and ensure adherence to schedule and budget;
Support CSIR business development through identifying energy industry services for the research group;
Support the energy industry research agenda (Energy Industry Support and Just Energy Transition Research).
Qualifications, skills and experience:
An Honours degree in energy economics, economics, science or engineering with at least six years’ working experience in the energy sector, of which three years’ should be in the green economy sector or energy industry development support or energy transition domain or energy-related projects in biogas, solar PV, wind, green hydrogen etc.
A Master’s degree will be advantageous;
Experience in the South African renewable energy industry / renewable energy sources;
Experience in an economic modelling, energy utility, government, consulting, or economic analysis environment;
Strong network in the public and private sector as links to the Green Economy/ Energy Industry/ Energy Transition contract R&D funding opportunities;
Ability to draft proposals, attract funding and lead project teams;
Experience in Computable General Equilibrium (CGE) or Social Accounting Matrices (SAM) modelling will be advantageous;
Experience in macro-economic impact analysis will be advantageous;
Experience with Small, Medium and Micro Enterprises will be advantageous.
