Job Description
Main purpose:
To produce relevant, exclusive and factually correct news reports and analysis for News24 and its national audience on court proceedings in Gauteng's high and lower courts.
Duties and Responsibilities:
Investigate and research original crime and court content and ideas for news, feature and analysis stories;
Report on breaking crime incidents, and from crime scenes and court as and when events happen;
Breaking developing crimes and court judgments as per News24’s processes;
Interview and report on the experiences of victims and witnesses of crime;
Report on and investigate the inner workings of the police, Hawks, metro police and NPA where necessary;
Report on the latest research and studies into crime and justice;
Write quality news and feature articles, adhering to strict deadlines and News24’s style;
Create target-market-specific articles and multi-media content;
Generate ideas for news and features stories on a daily basis;
Adhere to the quality, style and content standards as laid out and required by the particular publication; Comply with the requirements of the South African Press Code;
Cultivate and maintain a strong network of contacts in the South African Police Service, Hawks and National Prosecuting Authority;
Will be required to take photographs and shoot video on your mobile phone as and when required to enrich your reportage.
Live reporting into News24 live blogs on developing stories.
