Role Summary:
As a Corporate Finance Officer, you will work closely with a team of experienced accountants based in Luxembourg in order to perform the bookkeeping, accounting and analysis of corporate accounts. You will be asked to prepare KPIs, work on month-end closing and put together reports required by local regulators in order to ensure proper follow up of the performance of the business. Working in a multi-cultural, dynamic and complex environment, you will be asked to carry out duties in a professional manner in accordance with policies and procedures, legal/regulatory requirements, service levels and company standards so as to meet with Luxembourg Finance team expectations. You will assist the Luxembourg-based Finance team in reaching a level of excellence and thoroughness as expected by our clients, regulators and management.
Responsibilities:
Actively participate to month-end closing processes within different business models and countries. Each business model involves a certain level of complexity (Reporting standards, currency etc.);
Prepare daily KPI’s such as intra-day cash positions, Assets Under Management and regulatory capital requirements;
Improve financial status by analyzing results, monitoring variances, identifying trends and recommending actions to management;
Reconcile cash transactions and report/investigate any doubtful item;
Maintain and improve active database by entering, verifying, and backing up data;
Increase productivity by participating to the development of automated accounting applications and coordinating information requirements;
Protect operations by keeping financial information confidential;
Contribute to team efforts by accomplishing related results as needed;
Work with the Finance team in Luxembourg to produce the annual business plan and manage the monthly process for updating the forecast;
Produce financial/business KPI’s and requisite reports to provide a clear view of the company’s and individual teams’ performances;
Constantly improve and enhance your own skills by participating to courses, classes or trainings and show willingness to learn.
Requirements:
At least a Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance or Business Administration;
1 to 3 years of relevant experience within a Finance department and/or Reporting;
Proven exposure or interest in the Funds industry and related financial activities;
Good knowledge of Microsoft Excel (Formulas, formatting, pivot tables) with the willingness to learn;
Fluent in English (Written and spoken); Any other internationally spoken language is a plus (French being highly appreciated);
Able to meet tight deadlines in a complex environment;
High professional standards and able to evolve in a young, dynamic and multi-cultural environment;
Intellectually curious, quick learner and able to identify root causes of issues quickly.

Main Purpose of the Job
To promote a welcoming and professional branch image, through the efficient handling of clients, staff, and business associates’ queries, whether telephonically or by personal contact, and to fulfil all the administrative duties of the branch.
Key Responsibilities
Supporting our Agents with various administrative tasks;
Compilation of advertising material;
Compilation of brochures and portfolios;
Responsible for updating mandate boards and files, listing properties on the in-house PGP system, keeping the website up to date and Property 24 and Private Property featured listings;
Rental administration;
General office duties including the ordering of office supplies, stationery, general correspondence and filing;
Responsible for incoming and outgoing e-mail correspondence with clients, agents and staff;
Manage the switchboard and reception area;
Assist with walk-in clients in a warm and welcoming manner;
Manage the petty cash in the branch;
Conveyancing and sales administration activities.
Key Competencies
Excellent verbal and written communication skills with the ability to represent our brand in every interaction;
Good interpersonal skills, confident with a strong service orientation;
Have friendly, courteous and approachable demeanour;
Bilingual (English and Afrikaans);
Take telephonic messages efficiently and accurately;
The ability to work in a busy, pressurised environment with excellent organisational skills;
Attention to detail, accuracy and ability to handle correspondence effectively;
Working independently and the ability to take initiative when required is absolutely essential.
Place a high value on confidentiality and integrity.
Education & Experience
Matric;
Previous secretarial duties essential - with prior real estate experience an advantage.
Knowledge & Skills Required
Computer literacy (Ms Office, Internet explorer, Excel) and comfort with technology is essential.

A Principal Analyst Developer is a very knowledgeable, results-driven, experienced and high performing individual who has a vast amount of delivery experience at FNZ.
This role requires an expert evel knowledge of FNZ platform capabilities and technologies. From their experience, they will have worked across multiple FNZ clients and have a proven delivery record. They are extremely capable individuals who are regarded as experts within the Analyst Developer team.
They must have an exceptional ability to analyse complex system changes, design databases, write complex financial business logic and create slick web applications. Regarded as experts within FNZ, they will influence and support others to ensure that all system changes are developed to a high level of quality and best practice is adhered to.
Specific Role Responsibilities
Consultation & Collaboration
Collaborate with others across FNZ Group to ensure that solutions developed are robust, maintainable and in-line with the requirements;
Responsible for ensuring that code is designed and built in a reusable manner. Promote opportunities for cross-project system design / solutions.
As an expert, provide pro-active technical consultation to other developers and FNZ project teams.
Be a key authority on system design and architecture to influence best practice. Be able to validate and scope effort required for any project globally, objectively and accurately
Take accountability and be personally responsible for complex designs, development and product ownership
Analysis & Design
Work within the constraints of the feature/user story to define the underlying design required to deliver these changes
Ensure the solution is well defined and fit-for-purpose. It must meet the requirements and work end-to-end.
Provide solutions and recommendations for the resolution of technical issues that arise and ensure solutions meet the technical specs and design requirements;
Help design and build APIs and external system interfaces for integration into core FNZ products and third-party vendor applications;
Development
Highly mobile across the organisation, able to move as required across all FNZ projects and able to immediately add value
Interpret complex financial business requirements and translate into high-transactional, high-availability, secure, working systems;
Design and build the highly intuitive user interface and interactive financial tools required by financial advisers and investors;
Develop real-time transaction processing systems that support millions of trades every day in investment securities in multiple world markets;
Able to build high complexity features end-to-end
Expert in multiple system/technical areas of the FNZ platform, regarded as an SME in these areas.
Familiar with Information Security best practice and standards with the ability to apply these throughout technical development
Contributor to global non-client specific projects to advance key technical strategies across FNZ.
Quality
Establishes best practice for defect mitigation and resolution within their project team and in the wider solution centre.
Develops and inspires others to take a proactive and preventative approach to defect management.
Adheres to the defined procedures for code management, code reviews, coding standards, naming conventions and security standards;
Write automated unit tests for any newly created code; and
Perform manual testing to ensure any changes made to the system are of a high standard and the system hasn’t regressed.
Perform code reviews for developers on their own and different projects, inside the solution centre, to ensure that proposed changes meet quality and best practice standards.
Able to design new core system functionality or completely redesign existing ones.
Communication
Promote the development team both internally and externally. Ensure that creative solutions, tight code, tough problems solved are called out appropriately to the developer community, and where they lead to visible outcomes, to the broader FNZ teams and clients; and
Provide solution centre-wide training, as required, on topics of personal expertise.
Identifies gaps in knowledge and areas of improvement for integrations. Help to drive training and enforcement of standards in order to improve non-functional quality of integration solutions.
Able to prepare and lead technical workshops internally and/or involving clients and/or vendors.
Actively identifies and drives technical training in the solution centre. Has a global focus and finds ways to propagate knowledge around FNZ Group.
Leader of leaders - actively mentors and coaches other senior members of the development team, whether through formal line management or through another arrangement.
Leverages excellent verbal and written communication skills. Able to advise stakeholders and positively influence technical decisions both internally and externally.
Technology
Expert authority in C# and .NET – keeps actively up-to-date with progression in the technology and looks at ways to effectively bring it into use.
Proactively resolve technical (environmental, coding and testing) issues that impede development progress. Assist in the resolution of technical issues when requested by other developers; and
Create novel solutions to problems by incorporating cutting edge technology or concepts.
Experience Required
Industry Knowledge
First class bachelors degree or higher and/or equivalent experience;
Experience of working on large scale technology delivery projects and successfully delivering technology change as part of these projects;
Confident, and able to take a lead role in a delivery-focused environment;
Experience of working with different levels of stakeholders within a project environment;
Expert in the FNZ platform & technologies;
Independent, self-directing working style;
Ability to learn quickly in a dynamic fast-paced industry;
Enjoy working as part of a high-performance team;
Hard-working, innovative and takes pride in their work; and
Passionate about creating innovative solutions for customers.
Required Knowledge & Skills
Expert in Microsoft .NET development products, including .NET, C# and SQL Server;
Expert in web development, including ASP.NET, JavaScript and ReactJS;
Experience with the following legacy development products would be beneficial: ASP.NET MVC, VB.NET, legacy .NET Framework versions.
Understanding of financial products and markets;
Understanding of web services;
Familiar with code analysis or automated testing tools.

Job description:
POSITION SYNOPSIS:
The purpose of the role is to assist line management in meeting safety, health and environmental standards and implementing safety initiatives in their respective work areas, by verifying compliance to HSE systems during inspections, audits, investigations and leaderships interactions and interventions, specifically in the projects and construction environment.
REQUIREMENTS:
Serious contenders will have a Degree/BTECH/National Diploma in Safety Management together with 5 years’ experience in Mining Environment;
Blasting ticket or valid trade test will be advantegous;
SAMTRAC or COMSOC 1 & 2 certificates is essential;
In depth knowledge of the Mine Health and Safety Act (Act 29 of 1996), Occupational Health and Safety Act 93 of 1993 and other related legislation is essential;
Experience in Incident Cause Analysis Method (ICAM) methodology is essential;
Experience in contractor management processes is essential;
Computer literacy in MS Office Suite is essential;
A valid Code B driver’s License is essential
CORE ACCOUNTABILITIES:
Conduct 30, 45- and 90-days legal inspections;
Conduct internal audits of the system, process;
Discuss, record and signoff off findings/deviations in the inspection logbook;
Follow up and close out all preventative and corrective actions;
Update inspection schedule;
Monitor compliance to required controls, COP, standards, procedures and applicable legislation;
Analyse trends and report to line Managers;
Facilitate event investigations and ensure quality outcomes (MTC’s, LTI’s and RWC’s)
Assist Chief Safety Officer with DMRE reporting;
Investigate and submission of Significant Events, incidents, damages, hazards and complaints;
Carry out responsibilities in terms of HSE legal and regional requirements;
Challenge line and contractors on identified gaps (e.g. reporting, FRC compliance, risks and hazards, etc.);
Audit and verify the effective implementation of controls and compliance to legal and other requirements;
Assist in the analysis of Safety Statistics Identify specific learning’s relevant to the site and communicate as appropriate;
Carryout Safety campaigns.

Responsibilities
It will be expected of the successful candidate to:
Teach core modules in chemical engineering (e.g. Materials & energy balance, transport phenemona, process synthesis and analysis, chemical engineering design, environmental safety engineering, etc) at undergraduate and postgraduate levels in the Department;
Supervise final year undergraduate BEng project students, BEngHons/BScHons students;
Supervise masters and doctoral students if already holding a PhD degree.
Be actively involved in a research group/unit focusing on the application of concepts of chemical/process engineering in sustainable environment and water utilisation processes/sustainable and efficient energy processes/ advanced and applied materials/process design and optimisation and publish in leading accredited journals in the field;
Raise and manage additional funding from national and international funding agencies and industry to support his/her research activities and that of the group he/she associates with;
Expand existing research programmes or initiate new research programmes;
Perform assigned departmental duties (e.g. of an administrative nature).
Minimum Requirements
Lecturer
A BEng/BScEng degree in Chemical Engineering or closely related discipline from a university of which the undergraduate programme is registrable with Engineering Council of South Africa (ECSA);
A Masters’ degree in Chemical Engineering or closely related discipline that follows on the previous qualification;
Research experience in chemical engineering, in particular in application of concepts of chemical/process engineering in sustainable environment and water utilisation processes/sustainable and efficient energy processes/ advanced and applied materials/process design and optimisation;
Publications in accredited journals or conferences;
Industry related experience within the field.
Added Advantages And Preferences
Evidence of teaching experience (at least 1 year) in higher institution;
Preference will be given to candidates who have teaching and research expertise that complement the Department’s needs;
Preference will be given to candidates who already hold a PhD degree in Chemical Engineering or in a closely related discipline or at the final stage (e.g. 3 rd year) of his/her doctoral degree programme in Chemical Engineering or in a closely related discipline
Related industry work or consulting experience;
Candidates registered or registerable as Professional Engineer with ECSA;

