Role Description
This is an opportunity for an HR Administrator to contribute to the growth of a dynamic company within the financial industry.
You will have the opportunity to refine our HR process and procedures together with the HR Manager. The role is a great opportunity for a go-getter passionate about administration and organisation.
Job Specification
Record accurate data and personnel information to maintain a quality HR records management system in relation to the following:
Filing, storing and processing of all HR records and employee personal information;
HR records for internal & external audits;
Submissions of employee information for payroll processing;
Completion of UIF documentation;
Preparation of HR reports, letters and correspondences when required.
Apply correct application of leave rules and maintain accurate leave and absenteeism records;
Coordinate and monitor the administration of the hiring, onboarding and offboarding processes:
Placement of job adverts on BambooHR (internal & external);
Employment reference checks and pre-employment verifications;
Liaison with hiring managers & candidates during the hiring process;
Secure payments for specific accounts of external platforms or recruitment service providers.
Secure effectiveness in administering onboarding of new employees.
Coordinate/administer offboarding and retirement process;
Support the daily operations of the HR department i.t.o.:
Distribution of HR communications, HR policies and processes;
Respond to and resolve general HR queries;
Support to Social committee with election of new members and their internal functions;
Gifts i.t.o. long service awards & farewell functions.
Assist with administration of IOD and COIDA claims.
Prepare the evidence and witnesses to counter Disciplinary hearings and CCMA referrals.
Job Required Skills
Fluent in English and Afrikaans (specifically reading Afrikaans);
Professional Verbal and Written Communication skills;
Reliable with a high level of professionalism, discretion, confidentiality and sensitivity;
Time Management and able to work independently;
Prioritising & Planning; Able to use initiative and multi-task;
Ability to work under pressure and follow instructions;
Accuracy & Attention to detail;
Advanced skills in Microsoft Office
Qualification & Experience
Diploma in Human Resource management or equivalent related qualification
At least 3 years’ working experience and knowledge within an HR environment.
At least 2 years’ proven HR administration experience
Sage Payroll or other payroll systems experience will be advantageous
HRIS (Human Resources Information Systems) experience will be advantageous.

About The Job
The CSIR has a vacancy for Procurement Specialist. The incumbent is expected to support the Smart Places Hosted Programmes, the National Cleaner Production Centre (NCPC-SA) and the National Foundry Technology Network (NFTN). The two programmes support industry sectors to be more sustainable through the provision of technical services. The incumbent will be responsible for procurement of specialist services required to support the industry. This will also include supporting the roll-out of procurement for a large renewable energy project across South Africa in the next five years. The position is based in Pretoria.
Key Responsibilities
Learn the business needs and industry challenges of the NCPC-SA and NFTN;
Source goods and services, review and manage existing supplier relationship;
Document and assess the NCPC and NFTN business and sourcing objectives;
Track and report on spend patterns;
Support a supplier development programme to assist new suppliers to be considered for specialist contracts;
Determine the total value of identified commodities and report accordingly to management;
Source suppliers that meet the CSIR procurement criteria and ensure compliance to the CSIR’s B-BBEE policy and programme;
Manage procurement transactional services ensuring reduction in purchase order cycle times and tracking supplier performance against targets;
Assess and implement automation of processes to improve service delivery;
Expedite orders to monitor quality, on time deliveries, preferential procurement and savings;
Ensure effective and timely response to user calls related to orders and deliveries;
Keep abreast with business systems and new developments;
Manage procurement activities throughout the purchasing and supply chain;
Ensure that purchasing activities are provided in a fair, equitable, transparent, cost effective, efficient, and effective manner;
Build strategic, professional, and ethical relationships with other CSIR units and the Hosted Programmes suppliers;
Ensure buying activities support the CSIR’s supplier contracts and that the organisation’s strategic interests are considered in such relationships;
Report on relevant management information.
Qualifications, Skills, And Experience
A Bachelor’s degree or equivalent three-year purchasing qualification with at least five years’ experience in procurement.
Public sector procurement experience
Good understanding and experience of Total Cost of Ownership (TCO).
Report writing skills.
Supplier evaluation experience and thorough understanding of business processes.
Sourcing, buying, negotiation, planning and organising skills.
Contract management skills and e-procurement knowledge.
High degree of accuracy, attention to detail and problem-solving ability.
Ability to meet demanding deadlines and good interpersonal skills; and
Excellent communication skills and strong customer service focus.
Closing date: 15 March 2023
